  "id": "misdiagnosis",
  "term": "misdiagnosis",
  "definition": "Misdiagnosis is an incorrect diagnosis that can happen when one condition’s symptoms resemble those of another illness or are mimicked by a medical condition or drug effects. In mental health assessment, avoiding misdiagnosis involves looking at how symptoms change over days and weeks instead of judging only the person’s current symptoms.",
